.IX Title "AWS::SecureMediaDelivery::Secret 3"
.TH AWS::SecureMediaDelivery::Secret 3 "2025-11-03" "perl v5.34.1" "User Contributed Perl Documentation"
.\" For nroff, turn off justification.  Always turn off hyphenation; it makes
.\" way too many mistakes in technical documents.
.if n .ad l
.nh
.SH "NAME"
AWS::SecureMediaDelivery::Secret \- Manages cryptographic secrets for token signing
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.IX Header "SYNOPSIS"
.Vb 1
\&    use AWS::SecureMediaDelivery::Secret;
\&    
\&    # Native AWS Secrets Manager retrieval
\&    my $secret = AWS::SecureMediaDelivery::Secret\->new(
\&        stack_name => \*(AqMyStack\*(Aq,
\&        ttl        => 300,
\&    );
\&    
\&    # Custom secret retrieval
\&    my $secret = AWS::SecureMediaDelivery::Secret\->new(
\&        stack_name       => \*(AqMyStack\*(Aq,
\&        ttl              => 300,
\&        retrieve_mode    => \*(Aqcustom\*(Aq,
\&        retrieve_function => sub {
\&            my ($stack_name) = @_;
\&            return {
\&                primary => {
\&                    uuid  => \*(Aqcustom\-uuid\*(Aq,
\&                    value => \*(Aqcustom\-value\*(Aq,
\&                },
\&            };
\&        },
\&    );
\&    
\&    # Retrieve keys
\&    my $keys = $secret\->retrieve_keys();
\&    my $primary_key = $secret\->retrieve_keys(\*(Aqprimary\*(Aq);
.Ve
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
.IX Header "DESCRIPTION"
This class handles the retrieval and caching of secrets from \s-1AWS\s0 Secrets Manager
or custom sources for use in \s-1JWT\s0 token generation.
.SH "METHODS"
.IX Header "METHODS"
.SS "new(%args)"
.IX Subsection "new(%args)"
Creates a new Secret instance.
.IP "\(bu" 4
stack_name \- CloudFormation stack name (required)
.IP "\(bu" 4
ttl \- Time-to-live for cached secrets in seconds (required)
.IP "\(bu" 4
retrieve_mode \- 'native' for \s-1AWS\s0 Secrets Manager or 'custom' for custom function (default: 'native')
.IP "\(bu" 4
retrieve_function \- Custom function to retrieve secrets (CodeRef)
.IP "\(bu" 4
retrieve_function_args \- Arguments for custom retrieve function (ArrayRef)
.SS "init_sm_client(%params)"
.IX Subsection "init_sm_client(%params)"
Initialize \s-1AWS\s0 Secrets Manager client.
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    $secret\->init_sm_client(region => \*(Aqus\-east\-1\*(Aq);
.Ve
.SS "retrieve_keys($key_alias)"
.IX Subsection "retrieve_keys($key_alias)"
Retrieve cryptographic keys with caching.
.PP
.Vb 3
\&    my $all_keys = $secret\->retrieve_keys();
\&    my $primary = $secret\->retrieve_keys(\*(Aqprimary\*(Aq);
\&    my $secondary = $secret\->retrieve_keys(\*(Aqsecondary\*(Aq);
.Ve
.SS "get_key_value($key_alias)"
.IX Subsection "get_key_value($key_alias)"
Get the value of a specific key.
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    my $value = $secret\->get_key_value(\*(Aqprimary\*(Aq);
.Ve
.SS "get_key_uuid($key_alias)"
.IX Subsection "get_key_uuid($key_alias)"
Get the \s-1UUID\s0 of a specific key.
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    my $uuid = $secret\->get_key_uuid(\*(Aqprimary\*(Aq);
.Ve
.SS "validate_keys($keys)"
.IX Subsection "validate_keys($keys)"
Validate the format of retrieved keys (class method).
.PP
.Vb 1
\&    AWS::SecureMediaDelivery::Secret\->validate_keys($keys);
.Ve
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.IX Header "SEE ALSO"
AWS::SecureMediaDelivery::Token, AWS::SecureMediaDelivery::Session
